@3.8 Block IF
.
=3.8 BLOCK IF
.
=SYNTAX
.
:GP.IF <expr> THEN
:    ...
:GP.ELSEIF <expr> THEN
:    ...
:GP.ELSE
:    ...
:GP.ENDIF
.
=WHAT IT COSTS
.
.  ASM: GP.IF GP.ELSEIF GP.ELSE GP.ENDIF
.    ASM -- machine code in the GP runtime block. One GP keyword pays for the
.    whole block.
.
=DESCRIPTION
.
.  GP.IF
.      RULE: one per block, alone on its line, THEN required
.
.  GP.ELSEIF
.      RULE: any number of them, THEN required
.
.  GP.ELSE
.      RULE: optional, at most one
.
.  GP.ENDIF
.      RULE: required; without it the compile stops on STRUCTURE IMBALANCE
.
.  condition
.      RULE: a numeric expression
.
.The first true condition runs and nothing below it does, so there is no
.break to omit. A block whose conditions are all false and which has no
.GP.ELSE is skipped, which is not an error.
.
.There is no one-line form. GP.IF X > 5 THEN PRINT is a syntax error. Stock
.IF ... THEN is unchanged and is the one-line form.
.
.Blocks nest freely: inside each other, inside a GP.CASE body (SEC 3.2) and
.inside a GP.DO loop (SEC 3.1). Use GP.SELECT (SEC 3.2) where one value is
.compared against each alternative, and a block IF where each branch tests a
.different condition.
.
.A GOTO out of a block is safe. The condition is evaluated and consumed on
.the line it is written, so GP.ENDIF releases nothing. The block costs 14
.runtime bytes.
.
:GP.IF N < 0 THEN
:    PRINT "NEGATIVE"
:GP.ELSEIF N = 0 THEN
:    PRINT "ZERO"
:GP.ELSE
:    PRINT "POSITIVE"
:GP.ENDIF
.
=EXAMPLE PROGRAM
.
.  IF.EXP.BL -- runnable, in the GPC-BASIC folder
.
=SEE ALSO
.
>30|3.2 Multi-way branch
>29|3.1 Loops
